        {
          "id": 1677424426,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@johnthacker @geraldcombs \nI'm not sure what you mean. \ndissect_zbee_tlvs() is not a recursvie function, it calls dissect_zbee_tlv() several times (while there are unparsed bytes).",
          "author": {
            "id": 14240132,
            "username": "Stepan_C",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Stepan Chernousov",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6663133c08fb5f53f1a2540b74b4c590608777ec0d44c9ae1d6fb4edf8647284?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Stepan_C"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-04T09:23:24.572Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-05T01:28:33.186Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 267488160,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-12-05T01:28:33.186Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13526,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1677660046,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`dissect_zbee_tlv()` can call `dissect_global_tlv()` which can call `dissect_zbee_tlvs()` in two cases of encapsulated TLVs. A carefully crafted fuzzed packet can do this while advancing only the offset by two bytes each time `dissect_global_tlv()` is called (and the other functions only inspect the offset.) Apparently this can be enough to cause stack exhaustion, though it may depend on exact compiler options (such as not optimizing and thus not inlining, not omitting the frame pointer, etc.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-04T11:19:17.192Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-05T01:28:33.186Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 267488160,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-12-05T01:28:33.186Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13526,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1677697926,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks, I see. \nThere are no options here when these TLVs can be used several times in a frame (according ZigBee spec) and frame can't have both of encapsulated TLVs at the same time.",
          "author": {
            "id": 14240132,
            "username": "Stepan_C",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Stepan Chernousov",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
